A1. Famous trouble maker. ~ CUPID
A6. You can't do without this. ~ FOOD
A10. Often found in slot machines. ~ SLUG
A14. Angels are this way. ~ ALATE
A15. Always against something. ~ ANTI
A16. Here's a fishy one. ~ TUNA
A17. Doles (Ah there, Mr. Hopkins!). ~ METES
A18. Where backseat drivers drive you. ~ NUTS
A19. This makes us blue. ~ ANIL
A20. What no WPA worker ever does to himself. ~ EXERTS
A22. Siamese twins can't do this. ~ SEPARATE
A24. Russian inland sea. ~ ARAL
A26. What a Chinaman does to his ancestors. ~ REVERES
A27. This can be taken for granted. ~ BESTOWED
A31. Recession ink. ~ RED
A32. Where the corpse was found. ~ ALLEY
A33. You can make hay with this. ~ GRASS
A35. This is real hot. ~ SOL
A38. First cousin to a stork. ~ IBIS
A39. What motorists should do at grade crossings. ~ PAUSE
A40. This is barred, but not banned. ~ CAGE
A41. What every lass desires. ~ LAD
A42. Hollanders went crazy about this once. ~ TULIP
A43. Japan's first bite out of China—and what an appetite it developed! ~ COREA
A44. This makes the wheels go 'round. ~ COG
A45. Inquired—and no foolin'. ~ DEMANDED
A47. Sarcastic in a highbrow way. ~ SATIRIC
A51. What the law does to culprits—sometimes. ~ NABS
A52. This fellow is always on his way. ~ TRAVELER
A54. Water in a hurry. ~ RAPIDS
A58. Competent. ~ ABLE
A59. Something abstract in the concrete. ~ IDEA
A61. Never let this get the best of you. ~ RIVAL
A62. What the burglar toted off. ~ LOOT
A63. This man makes you sleepy. ~ SAND
A64. Poets' pet goddess. ~ ERATO
A65. Sea eagles—and we don't mean ocean hoppers. ~ ERNS
A66. What the cop did on his beat. ~ TROD
A67. Dumb Dora thinks this is something for campers to sleep in. ~ TENET

D1. A wise man's vehicle if you L it. ~ CAME
D2. This spiny shrub is a sticker. ~ ULEX
D3. Where baldness begins. ~ PATE
D4. What a radio comedian does with an old gag. ~ ITERATES
D5. What Fascists would like to do to Communists—and vice versa. ~ DESTROY
D6. This will keep you cool. ~ FAN
D7. A weight on your mind. ~ ONUS
D8. Fur-bearing, aquatic mammal—no, not Johnny Weissmuller. ~ OTTER
D9. What mobs do when the Black Maria arrives. ~ DISPERSE
D10. Gazed vacantly, like a glass eye. ~ STARED
D11. Pertaining to the moon. ~ LUNAR
D12. John L. Lewis and William Green will never do this, it seems. ~ UNITE
D13. Big blow-hards. ~ GALES
D21. This has teeth, but can't chew. ~ SAW
D23. Birds in a class by themselves. ~ AVES
D25. This isn't unlawful. ~ LEGAL
D27. What to do when the boat leaks. ~ BAIL
D28. Napoleon hated this place. ~ ELBA
