D34. A tree with the jitters. ~ ASPEN
D35. Variety of carnelian. ~ SARD
D36. Curved molding. ~ OGEE
D37. What every actor wants to play. ~ LEAD
D39. A prize-fighter by this name smells just the same. ~ PUGILIST
D40. What plotters do when they get together. ~ CONSPIRE
D42. What the nail did to sonny's pants. ~ TORE
D43. Where dancing interferes with dining. ~ CABARET
D44. Catlike critters. ~ CIVETS
D46. What ashes do to rugs. ~ MAR
D47. Radio comedy. ~ STALE
D48. A shady sort of place. ~ ARBOR
D49. Sharp claw. ~ TALON
D50. Fragrant wood—but not to moths. ~ CEDAR
